    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d722">

                <pb facs="0767" n="665" xml:id="pg665"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.11/1684: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China
                        (Johnson)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-03-10T18:00:00-05:00">March 10, 1933—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>80. Your 229, March 9, 5 p.m. Department considers it desirable that replies of
                    American, British and Italian Governments to the Chinese Government’s request
                    for further postponement of payment of their respective shares of Boxer
                    Indemnity payments synchronize as to time of transmission to the Chinese
                    Government and that they be similar as to the general attitude expressed
                    therein. Department therefore desires that you withhold your reply until the
                    replies of your British and Italian colleagues are ready for transmission.</p>
                <p>In the event that both the British and Italian Governments are prepared to reply
                    adversely, you are authorized to inform the Foreign Office of the attitude of
                    the American Government as indicated in Department’s 47, February 11, 2 p.m. In
                    the event that either the British or Italian Governments is agreeable to a
                    further postponement of payments, please so inform the Department and await
                    further instructions.</p>
                <p>Department suggests that at your discretion you discuss matter along above lines
                    with your British and Italian colleagues, pointing out your view that early
                    reply appears to be desirable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
